 start=time.perf_counter();r=json.loads((PUBLIC/'G_direct_results.json').read_text());checks=json.loads((PUBLIC/'separate_check.json').read_text());attempt=json.loads((PUBLIC/'attempt.json').read_text());ledger=json.loads((RAW/'production/ledger.json').read_text());manifest=json.loads((PUBLIC/'local_raw_manifest.json').read_text());final=[v for v in r['population_estimates'] if v['time']==.01];initial=[v for v in r['population_estimates'] if v['time']==0];scoring=json.loads((PUBLIC/'scoring_attempt.json').read_text());ref=setup(160)['reference'];events=sum(v['events'] for v in ledger['records']);margin=r['paired_tick_checks'][0]['margin'];ci=lambda v:'['+', '.join(f'{x:.6g}' for x in v)+']'
 lines=['# MG183 G population pilot results','', 'This short pilot supports the population-scale explanation for poor G visibility. With concentrations and kinetics held fixed, the estimated G feature became easier to distinguish from background fluctuations as the token population increased. At model time 0.01, the planned approximate mean-contrast intervals included zero at Omega10 but excluded zero at Omega40 and Omega160. The limited finer-tick check at Omega160 passed its predefined tolerance, so tick size was not the dominant explanation for this short-time result. This does not establish sustained G persistence: there were only four replicates per condition, and the run ended before the previously difficult time 0.1 and later regimes.','', '## Completion and unchanged design','', f"All 24 registered jobs completed, with no scientific retries, replacements or omitted jobs. Wall time was {attempt['elapsed_seconds']/3600:.6g} hours and charged worker time {attempt['charged_worker_seconds']/3600:.6g} hours, below the three-hour wall and 24-worker-hour caps. Eight workers were used, with one numerical-library thread each. The sampler processed {events:,} accepted sampling marks, with common paired events counted once. The initial estimate was optimistic under parallel load; the approved caps were retained.", '', 'PI approval, source and canonical-input hashes, criteria and collision-checked fresh seeds were published at `7826e67` before scientific draws. The initial sandbox background launcher exited before creating a scientific attempt; its record remains. The persistent launcher started the one scientific attempt, which completed. No criteria changed after outcomes.','', 'The population grid was Omega10,40,160 on the same 500 sites, with four prepared and four species-mass-matched homogeneous replicates per population. Initial integer counts were rebuilt from unrounded concentrations, with A/B normalizers scaled consistently. All species and finite reservoirs were retained; no G reaction rate or measurement amplitude was increased. Omega160 jobs supplied paired ticks 0.0001 and 0.00002; their coarse marginals also supplied that population cell. The common scientific horizon was T=0.01, sampled every 0.001.','', '## Direct G result','', 'The observable is the signed projection of the centered G concentration field onto its fixed, unrounded initial G feature. It measures a localized spatial contrast, including the reference dip in G, not total G abundance or a newly fitted particle score. The prepared center is known; no alignment search, X/Y substitute or learned observer was used. All population-table results below use the coarse tick 0.0001.','', '| Omega | Prepared mean G projection | Homogeneous mean | Prepared-minus-control mean, approximate 95% CI | Control SD | Mean contrast / control SD |','|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|---:|']
 for v in final:lines.append(f"| {v['omega']} | {v['prepared']['mean']:.6g} | {v['control']['mean']:.6g} | {v['difference']['estimate']:.6g}, {ci(v['difference']['ci95'])} | {v['control']['sd']:.6g} | {v['control_sd_snr']:.6g} |")
 lines+=['', 'These are the registered Welch t intervals for two independent groups of four, with small-sample distribution assumptions. The ratio in the last column is descriptive and estimated from the same small groups; it is not a calibrated single-particle detection probability or a qualified signal-to-noise bound.','', 'The Omega10 interval crossing zero means this pilot did not separate its prepared and control means reliably under that interval calculation; it does not show that G was absent. The Omega40/160 positive intervals support a visible ensemble G contrast in these tested conditions. Mean intervals overlap across populations, so this is not evidence that the underlying G concentration was made larger.','', 'Estimated control dispersion fell from 0.392859 at Omega10 to 0.119676 at Omega40 and 0.114758 at Omega160 at T=0.01. This supports reduced noise overall, but the last two estimates are nearly equal; four controls cannot establish precise inverse-square-root scaling or reliably order their variances. At T=0.005 the corresponding SD estimates were 0.261702, 0.101301 and 0.0436886. The change with observation time is a reason to test the later regime rather than extrapolate this result.','', '![Direct G contrast and background fluctuation estimates](MG183_G_population_summary.png)','', '## Initial quantization and mean-field context','', '| Omega | Initial prepared-minus-control projection |','|---:|---:|']
 for v in initial:lines.append(f"| {v['omega']} | {v['difference']['estimate']:.6g} |")
