 for v in r['paired_tick_checks']:lines.append(f"| {v['condition']} | {v['time']:.6g} | {v['difference']['mean']:.6g} | {ci(v['difference']['ci95'])} | EQUIVALENT IN SCOPE |")
 lines+=['', 'Thus reducing the tick by a factor of five did not materially change the mean G projection at Omega160 within this short-horizon tolerance. This is not proof of exact continuum accuracy, agreement of every field, or tick equivalence at later times or other untested observables. The tick comparison passed; the population arm was an estimation pilot and has no registered binary persistence verdict.','', '## Verification, resources and data retention','', f"Separate analysis passed {checks['marginal_endpoints']} common-boundary marginal endpoint reconstructions, {checks['coarse_or_single_reservation_checks']} coarse/single reservation checks, {checks['RNG_continuity_checks']} RNG continuity checks and {checks['ordered_sentinel_traces']} chronological sentinel traces covering {checks['ordered_sentinel_events']:,} events. All 33 population/time estimates and four paired tick intervals were recomputed from explicitly centered fields. Maximum mean and CI differences were {checks['max_projection_mean_difference']:.6g} and {checks['max_CI_difference']:.6g}. Fine reservations were chronologically replayed in sentinel segments; they were not all independently traced. Shared data, model equations, Student references and the same author limit independence; this is not external replication.", '', f"Scoring took {scoring['elapsed_seconds']:.6g} seconds and separate verification {checks['elapsed_seconds']:.6g} seconds, within the 600-second analysis allowance. Full raw observations, histograms, RNG checkpoints, availability states and sentinel traces occupy {manifest['total_bytes']/1e6:.6g} MB locally in `local_raw/MG183_G_population`. Only compact summaries, mean/SD profiles, source and manifests are public. No full raw archive is uploaded.", '', '## Interpretation and recommended next step','', 'Your population-size suspicion now has direct support from the actual rule engine: larger populations improved short-time G visibility while a finer tick made a comparatively small difference in the specified mean measurement. The implementation audit found no G normalization or instantaneous drift mismatch. That supports investigating population noise before further observer refinement or G-specific kinetic changes.','', 'The next scientific question is whether the improvement survives to T=0.1, the first previously problematic G-noise regime. I recommend preparing a focused later-time comparison of Omega10 and Omega160, retaining prepared/control replication, direct G measurements and an appropriately bounded numerical check. Use the measured parallel costs for its budget; this pilot ran slower than the original one-job forecast. No longer run is started or authorized here.','', 'Even a successful later-time visibility comparison would not by itself prove full G/X/Y particle persistence. Known-center ensemble contrast, individual continuity, spontaneous-core identification and physical interpretation are separate claims. Four replicates do not qualify detection error rates, population variance scaling or rare failures. MG183 short-pilot reporting is complete; PI closure is pending. Earlier MG163 and observer verdicts remain unchanged, and long-horizon G viability remains open.']
